# Bilingual FA/EN layout

When owner-facing prose mixes **Persian and English**, Latin on the same line as Persian breaks RTL/LTR in Cursor chat — **even inside backticks**.

- **Own-line English (primary):** paths, commands, rule ids, npm scripts, URLs, and status labels on their **own line**, under **جزئیات** / **Details**, or in a fenced block.
- **Persian lines = zero Latin letters.** Backticks mid-sentence are not enough.
- **Cursor chat default (2026-08-23):** prefer **English** owner replies — this UI left-aligns RTL and does not present Persian correctly. Persian only if the owner asks that turn; bilingual habit is mitigation only, not an RTL fix.
- Does **not** replace the shared reporting rules or `owner-facing-sensors`. Does **not** apply to English-only replies.

Before send (Persian draft): `assertBilingualFaEnLayout` on the text.

Gate: `src/lib/bilingual-fa-en-layout.ts` (`assertBilingualFaEnLayout`).

